-- #1111 A-2.4 MIRROR PROBE (MODULE arm) -- the severity-ladder half of this unit.
--
-- A-2.4 turns two exit-1 rejections into exit-0 acceptances (#1257, #1258).  Per
-- AGENTS.md, "does this fix turn a path that returned NOTHING into one that returns
-- SOMETHING? If so, the new something is UNTESTED BY CONSTRUCTION" -- every
-- pre-existing fixture covered the rejecting case, so none of them can fail if the
-- fix over-widens and starts accepting things it must not.
--
-- So this fixture is the mirror: BOTH re-keyed tables' diagnostics, on GENUINE
-- defects, with NO same-name interface anywhere in the graph.  Both must still fire.
--   * `impl Alpha ET` defines `afoo` and NOT `abar` -- genuinely incomplete
--     (T-INCOMPLETE-IMPL, via `universeIfaceRequiredRef`).
--   * `impl Graded Q` heads a graded interface (slot 0 `Row`) with `Q`, whose slot 0
--     is a plain `Type` -- genuinely wrong-kinded (T-IMPL-KIND-MISMATCH, via
--     `universeIfaceParamKinds`).
--   * `impl Ord GT2` omits `compare` -- the same T-INCOMPLETE-IMPL diagnostic, but
--     against a PRELUDE interface, so the key that has to meet is
--     `ifaceTabKey (OriginModule "core") "Ord"` on BOTH sides.  Added by adversarial
--     review of this unit: until then NO committed fixture drove the prelude
--     population of `universeIfaceRequiredRef` in the REJECTING direction (the
--     bystander fixture's complete `impl Display ET` cannot -- a miss and a hit both
--     yield `[]` there), so core's whole write side could have stopped meeting its
--     read side and every fixture in the tree would still have been green.
--
-- The `gthen q f = gthen q f` body is deliberate: a body that CONSTRUCTS a `Q` drags
-- in an unrelated `Num`-on-a-quantified-tyvar diagnostic, which would let this
-- fixture keep passing on the wrong diagnostic if the kind check ever went quiet.
import alphamod.{Alpha, afoo}
import gradedmod2.{Graded, gthen}

data ET = MkET

impl Alpha ET where
  afoo e = 1

data Q a b = MkQ a b

impl Graded Q where
  gthen q f = gthen q f

-- The PRELUDE half.  `Ord`'s only required method is `compare` (stdlib/core.mdk:137-162
-- declares seven; `lt`/`gt`/`lte`/`gte`/`min`/`max` all carry default bodies), so an
-- impl supplying only `lt` is genuinely incomplete and must say so.
-- `impl Eq GT2` is present ON PURPOSE: `Ord a requires Eq a`, and without it this
-- fixture would also carry an unrelated superclass diagnostic that could keep it
-- passing if the completeness check itself ever went quiet.
data GT2 = MkGT2

impl Eq GT2 where
  eq a b = True

impl Ord GT2 where
  lt a b = False
